       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 4000 mg four times daily is 16,000 mg/day. No indication supports that dose, and it is in the range where serious toxicity is expected: GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS depression. A normal 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function has no physiologic reason to tolerate it.\n\nIf you want to go ahead, you could:\n- **Call pharmacy or your attending.** If there is a real reason for an unusual dose, they can review it and enter it through an override pathway with the right safeguards.\n- **Pick a standard dose.** I can enter 400, 600, or 800 mg PO four times daily (up to 3,200 mg/day) right away.\n- **Tell me what you're treating.** If pain or inflammation control is the goal, I can help you think through options, such as scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen.\n\nIf the patient has already taken a large amount of ibuprofen, contact Poison Control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) or toxicology."
